cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "RAG Evaluation Lab: Grounding, Citations and Regression Testing"
message: "If you refer to this work, please cite it as below."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Akor
    given-names: George
repository-code: "https://github.com/Jupiter-Plantagenet/rag-evaluation-lab"
abstract: >-
  A self-directed research-engineering case study in evaluating document-grounded
  retrieval-augmented generation. The repository implements an inspectable
  evaluation and regression-testing harness rather than a chatbot. It reports
  retrieval, answer, citation and system metrics separately instead of blending
  them into a single quality score; every published metric is deterministic,
  computed without consulting a model. It captures one structured trace per case
  recording the retrieved chunks and scores, the exact context the model was
  given, the parsed claims and the citations resolved back to character spans in
  a named source document. Failures are classified automatically from those trace
  signals under a fixed, cause-ordered taxonomy, and confirmed development-split
  failures are converted into regression tests that run offline with no model
  credentials. A deliberately simple baseline pipeline is compared against an
  improved pipeline whose interventions were selected from an observed failure
  distribution on the development split, using paired-bootstrap confidence
  intervals, and evaluated once on a held-out split that was frozen beforehand
  and is checksummed in the repository. Model-assisted grading is not
  implemented: no result depends on an LLM judge, and citation metrics establish
  that a citation resolves to a passage the model was shown rather than that the
  passage entails the claim. Evaluated on one synthetic corpus with one embedding
  model and one generation model; it is a case study, not a benchmark.
keywords:
  - retrieval-augmented generation
  - evaluation
  - retrieval metrics
  - citation resolution
  - regression testing
  - reproducibility
license: MIT
version: 0.1.0
